    <mj-text
      padding="10px 12px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Safety before streaming
      </h2>
    </mj-text>

    <mj-text padding="10px 12px 16px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What’s happening?</strong> The UAE governemnt have been issuing <a href="https://www.timeoutdubai.com/news/emergency-phone-alert" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">mobile alerts</a> through the National Early Warning System to keep residents and visitors' informed about the ongoing Israel-US and Iran tensions. The geo-targeted notifications, sent directly to phones, provide real-time safety instructions, including when to seek shelter. Agencies including the National Emergency Crisis and Disaster Management Authority (NCEMA) and the Ministry of Interior say the system is designed to deliver urgent guidance swiftly and ensure public safety.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>No filming: </strong>Authorities warn against prioritising social media <a href="https://gulfnews.com/uae/emergencies/uae-warns-against-filming-during-emergency-alerts-says-violators-face-legal-action-1.500462620" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">filming over safety</a> during emergency alerts, with violators facing legal accountability. The Ministry of Interior (MoI) reported residents stopping vehicles or leaving homes to record videos post-notification. Authorities emphasised that alerts are issued solely to protect the public, instructing immediate sheltering indoors or in secure locations until an "all clear" signal. Drivers must continue to destinations without roadside stops.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Emergency hotline: </strong> The MoI reminded residents that the national emergency hotline 999 is reserved strictly for genuine emergencies. Residents are urged to avoid spreading unverified information online, keep phone lines free for critical cases, and follow updates from official sources to support the country’s coordinated emergency response.</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="10px" />
