        <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Consular services halted
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">The US Embassy in Abu Dhabi and the US Consulate General in Dubai are closed, and services <a href="https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/usisrael-conflict-on-iran-escalates-on-day-5-uae-affirms-right-to-selfdefence-1.500462647" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">cannot be provided</a> in those facilities until further notice. Major attractions like Dubai Parks and Resorts, Global Village, and Ain Dubai remain closed due to regional security concerns from US-Israeli strikes on Iran. Malls, including Dubai Mall, and essential services <a href="https://gulfnews.com/business/tourism/emaar-confirms-communities-malls-and-projects-operating-normally-across-dubai-1.500462820" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">operate normally</a>; no public holidays today.</p>
</mj-text>

<mj-divider
  border-style="dashed"
  border-width="1px"
  border-color="lightgrey"
  padding="0px 12px 4px 12px"
/>

<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Tracks of preparedness
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Etihad Rail, coordinating with Abu Dhabi’s ADCMC, operated three exceptional passenger trains from Al Ghuwaifat Station (bordering Saudi Arabia) to Al Faya Station, <a href="https://gulfnews.com/uae/transport/inside-etihad-rails-mission-how-over-350-uae-passengers-returned-from-saudi-arabia-in-3-trains-1.500462838" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">safely transporting</a> over 350 UAE residents home amid regional travel disruptions. The service, running ahead of the official passenger rail launch, adhered to full safety protocols without affecting freight operations, showcasing the UAE’s emergency transport readiness.</p>
</mj-text>

<mj-divider
  border-style="dashed"
  border-width="1px"
  border-color="lightgrey"
  padding="0px 12px 4px 12px"
/>

<mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
    Dubai cools down
  </h2>
</mj-text>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Dubai faces partly cloudy to cloudy skies with chances of scattered rainfall and <a href="https://www.khaleejtimes.com/uae/weather/march-4-2026" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #102341; color: black;">cooler temperatures</a> peaking at 34°C, dipping to 23°C overnight. Light to moderate winds may freshen, causing blowing dust and reduced visibility, with fog alerts in place. Rough seas are expected in the Arabian Gulf, with wave heights reaching up to 7 feet.</p>
</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
